@page "/HowItWorks"
@using InvestmentTaxCalculator.ViewModel

<PageTitle>How the calculator works</PageTitle>

<div class="container-fluid py-4 how-it-works">
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-lg-10 mx-auto">
            <div class="page-header">
                <h1 class="page-title">How the calculator works</h1>
                <p class="page-subtitle">How this app applies the UK share matching rules to your trades, with worked examples</p>
            </div>

            <div class="section">
                <p>
                    The general rules are explained well elsewhere. These guides cover how <strong>this app</strong> applies them:
                    which trades it groups together, which figures it uses, and in what order it matches trades. You can then
                    check its results against your own working or another calculator.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="section">
                <h2 class="section-title" id="matching-order">The order trades are matched in</h2>
                <p>
                    Each disposal is matched against acquisitions of the same share in this order. Each step only uses the
                    shares that earlier steps left unmatched:
                </p>
                <ol>
                    <li><strong><a href="HowItWorks/same-day-rule" class="link-styled">Same day</a>:</strong> shares bought on the same day as the disposal (TCGA 1992 s105(1)).</li>
                    <li><strong><a href="HowItWorks/30-day-rule" class="link-styled">Next 30 days</a>:</strong> shares bought in the 30 days after the disposal, earliest first (s106A(5)).</li>
                    <li><strong><a href="HowItWorks/section-104-pool" class="link-styled">Section 104 pool</a>:</strong> shares held before the disposal, at their average cost (s104).</li>
                    <li><strong><a href="HowItWorks/short-sales" class="link-styled">Later acquisitions</a>:</strong> if all of that is not enough (a short sale), shares bought later, earliest first (s105(2)).</li>
                </ol>
                <p>
                    The app runs each step for <em>every</em> share before it moves on to the next step. For example, all
                    same-day matches are made before any 30-day match. A purchase that a same-day match uses up is no longer
                    available to an earlier disposal's 30-day match. In every step, fees are included in the figures as
                    described in <a href="HowItWorks/net-proceeds" class="link-styled">Net proceeds and fees</a>.
                </p>
                <p>
                    "The same share" means the same share identity. Trades with the same ISIN are treated as one share even
                    when the ticker differs, for example with an exchange suffix. A reused ticker with a different ISIN is
                    kept separate. You can link old and new tickers yourself, for example after a NewCo reorganisation. See the
                    <a href="https://github.com/alexpung/UK-Investment-tax-calculator/wiki/Share-identities" class="link-styled" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">share identities wiki page</a>.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="section">
                <h2 class="section-title">Guides</h2>
                <div class="row g-4">
                    @foreach (var guide in HowItWorksGuides.All)
                    {
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="card feature-card">
                                <div class="card-body">
                                    <h3 class="h5 card-title"><a href="@guide.PageAddress" class="link-styled">@guide.Title</a></h3>
                                    <p class="card-text mb-0">@guide.Summary</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    }
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="section">
                <h2 class="section-title" id="check-workings">Checking the workings in the app</h2>
                <p>After you run a calculation, these pages show each step:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><a href="TradeMatchPage" class="link-styled">Trade Matches</a> lists every match with its type (same day, bed and breakfast, Section 104, cover short selling), its quantities, proceeds and allowable cost.</li>
                    <li><a href="CalculationViewPage" class="link-styled">Disposal Summary</a> shows each combined trade, how many of its shares each rule matched, and its proceeds, allowable cost and gain.</li>
                    <li><a href="ImportedTradesDataPage" class="link-styled">Imported Trades</a> shows each broker trade with its gross and net amount.</li>
                    <li><a href="Section104DataPage" class="link-styled">Section 104 Data</a> shows the pool's history for each share.</li>
                    <li><a href="CgtYearlyTaxSummaryPage" class="link-styled">CGT Yearly Summary</a> gives the totals for your tax return, using net proceeds.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h2 class="h5 card-title">Further reading</h2>
                    <ul class="mb-0">
                        <li>
                            <a href="https://github.com/alexpung/UK-Investment-tax-calculator/wiki" class="link-styled" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Project wiki</a>
                            has design notes for this app, with references to the legislation and HMRC manuals, including
                            <a href="https://github.com/alexpung/UK-Investment-tax-calculator/wiki/Traded-Financial-Options" class="link-styled" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">options</a> and
                            <a href="https://github.com/alexpung/UK-Investment-tax-calculator/wiki/Future-Contracts" class="link-styled" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">futures</a>,
                            which follow the same matching steps with some extra rules.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <a href="https://cgtvisualiser.co.uk/guides/" class="link-styled" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CGT Visualiser guides</a>
                            are plain-English explanations of the general rules. It is an independent site that is not connected
                            with this app.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            HMRC's own guidance on the matching order is
                            <a href="https://www.gov.uk/hmrc-internal-manuals/capital-gains-manual/cg51555" class="link-styled" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CG51555</a>.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="alert alert-warning alert-custom" role="alert">
                <strong>Not tax advice.</strong> These guides describe how the software calculates its figures. They are not
                tax, legal or financial advice. The app does not handle every exception in tax law. You are responsible for
                checking what you report.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
